  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...No significant weather concerns this week.\n\nHigh pressure centered near the Ohio and Tennessee Valleys will sag \ninto the Gulf Coast states. A weak cold front will pass through the \nregion tonight, and then Canadian high pressure builds into the \nNortheast on Tuesday. That high will eventually move offshore as the \nweek progresses.\n\nThe front that will pass through the region tonight will pass \nthrough dry, and high temperatures on Tuesday will be a few \ndegrees cooler compared to today. Some patchy fog may develop \nlate tonight, however, as the drier air may not filter down \nuntil Tuesday afternoon. As the week progresses, high \ntemperatures will warm into the upper 60s and low 70s, and then \ninto the mid 70s or so by Friday. Temperatures will still be \nslightly above normal for next weekend, but a bit cooler \ncompared to Friday. The next chance for precipitation does not \ncome until at least next Sunday or perhaps later. A dry stretch \nof weather is ahead.",
